/*
Problem: Odd Even Linked List
Platform: LeetCode (LC 328)
Topic: Linked List / Two Pointers

---------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

Rearrange the linked list so that:

1. All nodes at odd positions come first.
2. All nodes at even positions come after them.

NOTE:

Positions are considered (1st, 2nd, 3rd...)
NOT the node values.

---------------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5

Odd-position nodes:

1 → 3 → 5

Even-position nodes:

2 → 4

Final list:

1 → 3 → 5 → 2 → 4

---------------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Maintain three pointers:

odd

Points to the current odd-position node.

--------------------------------

even

Points to the current even-position node.

--------------------------------

temp

Stores the head of the even list,
so we can attach it after all odd nodes.

---------------------------------------------------------

Initially:

odd  = head

even = head->next

temp = even

---------------------------------------------------------

While both even and even->next exist:

Step 1:

Connect odd node to the next odd node.

odd->next = even->next

Move odd forward.

--------------------------------

Step 2:

Connect even node to the next even node.

even->next = odd->next

Move even forward.

Repeat.

---------------------------------------------------------

Finally:

Attach the even list after the odd list.

odd->next = temp

---------------------------------------------------------

Example:

1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5

Initially:

Odd:

1

Even:

2

--------------------------------

Iteration 1

Odd:

1 → 3

Even:

2 → 4

--------------------------------

Iteration 2

Odd:

1 → 3 → 5

Even:

2 → 4

--------------------------------

Attach:

1 → 3 → 5 → 2 → 4

Done.

---------------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Every iteration:

• skips one node for odd pointers

• skips one node for even pointers

Thus both odd and even chains
are formed independently.

Finally we connect them.

---------------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity:

O(n)

Every node is visited once.

---------------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity:

O(1)

Only pointers are used.

---------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* oddEvenList(ListNode* head) {

        // Empty list or single node
        if (head == NULL || head->next == NULL)
            return head;

        ListNode* odd = head;
        ListNode* even = head->next;

        // Save the head of the even list
        ListNode* temp = even;

        while (even != NULL &&
               even->next != NULL) {

            // Link odd nodes
            odd->next = even->next;
            odd = odd->next;

            // Link even nodes
            even->next = odd->next;
            even = even->next;
        }

        // Append even list after odd list
        odd->next = temp;

        return head;
    }
};
